Exactly three fields: `aid` (string), `wid` (string), `sections` (array of `{index, label, block_count}` — the raw `meta.sections`). **It is written but never read anywhere** (whole-file grep shows only those two lines; not even a reset on navigation). No other part of the app observes the reader's current section — the active chapter exists only as the `.nav-item.active` class (app.js:353-354), and the current idx is never stored in a variable or in the hash. If you add a dictionary panel you will need to either extend `readerState` with `idx` (write it in `loadSection`) or read `location.hash`.

