## Gotchas worth knowing before writing code
- `renderReader` and `runArchaism` both wipe `$view().innerHTML`, and `loadSection` wipes `#text.innerHTML` — any listener must be delegated on a surviving ancestor (`#text` itself survives section switches; `.reader-pane`/`$view()` survive everything).
- `readerState` is currently dead state; nothing resets it when leaving the reader.
- The reader payload has no word offsets/lemmas: `b.text` is one escaped string per block, and the section endpoints are `/api/text/{aid}/{wid}/section/{idx}` (blocks) and `/api/text/{aid}/{wid}/sections` (TOC). Any per-word dictionary lookup or annotation anchoring needs either client-side tokenization (matching the existing `esc()` output, which would break the current `textContent`-only render) or a new backend field.
- Existing style conventions to match: small-caps `--font-meta` for apparatus, `var(--radius)` 2px corners, hairline `var(--rule)` borders, one accent, `toast()` for feedback, `esc()` for every interpolated string.
